    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9189f79_6060a57c",
        "filename": "runtime/vdex_file.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 220,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-28T04:47:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you really need this check? A vdex file is loaded in one of the two ways:\n\n1. Loaded together with the oat file. In this case, the dex magic is checked [here](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:art/runtime/oat/oat_file.cc;l\u003d943;drc\u003d98797c2e6739910998c05a4ec0bc835690dcc76f).\n\n2. Loaded alone. In this case, the dex magic is checked [here](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:art/runtime/oat/oat_file.cc;l\u003d1784;drc\u003da7d85a831f0a330ce9914c57ae146fc03193451c).\n\nSince you have changed the magic check logic in this CL, cdex will fail the check in both cases.\n\nI suggest to leave this Vdex::IsValid unchanged and just add a test.",
      "parentUuid": "a37da09e_d7c8e7d4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 215,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 220,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c86911482ee8f63a5fcef1871dc5f43979e78b5e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d46ba7f1_88d09efc",
        "filename": "runtime/vdex_file.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 220,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-28T04:56:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One way to test this is through `OatFileAssistant`, in `OatFileAssistantTest`. An example can be found [here](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:art/runtime/oat/oat_file_assistant_test.cc;l\u003d762;drc\u003da7d85a831f0a330ce9914c57ae146fc03193451c). The test uses a helper function `GenerateOdexForTest` that calls dex2oat, with a compressed dex file as an input, to generate an authentic vdex file that contains a dex file.\n\nThe challenge is that `--compact-dex-level` is ignored by dex2oat. Otherwise, it would be easy to generate a vdex containing cdex by passing `--compact-dex-level\u003dfast` as the `extra_args` argument.",
      "parentUuid": "b9189f79_6060a57c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 215,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 220,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c86911482ee8f63a5fcef1871dc5f43979e78b5e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad2ce464_faaaeef2",
        "filename": "runtime/vdex_file.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 220,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-28T05:04:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks fragile to me to rely on VdexFile users to do the checks and leave VdexFile itself behaving wrong, but if others think that\u0027s ok then I\u0027ll delete this.\n\nI\u0027d still appreciate guidance on the test.",
      "parentUuid": "b9189f79_6060a57c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 215,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 220,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c86911482ee8f63a5fcef1871dc5f43979e78b5e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4379b68_0004473f",
        "filename": "runtime/vdex_file.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 220,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-28T05:10:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, didn\u0027t see the last reply from Jiakai. Yes, it sounds a bit complicated to make dex2oat output cdex, or do a full integration test. I\u0027m hoping it\u0027s relatively trivial to construct a test fixture directly in memory, for someone familiar with this code.",
      "parentUuid": "ad2ce464_faaaeef2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 215,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 220,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c86911482ee8f63a5fcef1871dc5f43979e78b5e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f03aef6_fa5b62d4",
        "filename": "runtime/vdex_file.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 220,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-28T05:56:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks inconsistant that so many checks on the dex file are on the VdexFile user side, while only one of them is duplicated on the VdexFile side. I think this inconsitancy hurts maintainability. Anyway, let\u0027s wait for others\u0027 inputs.\n\nIn terms of testing, if it\u0027s complicated to make dex2oat output cdex, what about\noverwriting the magic with \"cdex001\\0\" (through `pwrite` or something like that) after calling dex2oat? `oat_file_assistant_test.cc` may not be the best place to test this because it\u0027s not trivial to get the rejection reason from OatFileAssistant. `oat_file_test.cc` looks like a better place. The helper function `GenerateOdexForTest` is also available there, and you can check the `error_msg` returned from `OatFile::Open`/`OatFile::OpenFromVdex`, to make sure you hit [this line](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:art/runtime/oat/oat_file.cc;l\u003d945;drc\u003d98797c2e6739910998c05a4ec0bc835690dcc76f) and [this line](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:art/runtime/oat/oat_file.cc;l\u003d1785;drc\u003da7d85a831f0a330ce9914c57ae146fc03193451c).",
      "parentUuid": "a4379b68_0004473f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 215,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 220,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c86911482ee8f63a5fcef1871dc5f43979e78b5e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ea11b49_dec92ab6",
        "filename": "runtime/vdex_file.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 220,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
